Subject: [PATCH] programs/fuzz: initialise PSA once in the X.509 fuzzers

fuzz_x509crl, fuzz_x509csr and fuzz_x509crt called psa_crypto_init() and
mbedtls_psa_crypto_free() around every input, so each input paid for the
key-slot setup and the entropy poll + CTR_DRBG seeding (about 160k wasm
instructions, 47-97 % of the per-input cost). Parsing and the _info()
printers never draw random numbers, so do the initialisation once in
LLVMFuzzerInitialize() and keep it. The per-input psa_crypto_init() stays
as an early-out no-op (and keeps fuzz_onefile.c, which does not call
LLVMFuzzerInitialize, working); keys imported while parsing are still
destroyed by mbedtls_x509_*_free(), now while PSA is still up.

Upstream context: Mbed-TLS/mbedtls#10932 (open) moves psa_crypto_init() in
fuzz_client/fuzz_dtlsclient only; #10857 (open, new harnesses) and #11052 /
#11056 (open, new tls13_server / psa_crypto fuzzers) do not touch these files.

diff --git a/programs/fuzz/fuzz_x509crl.c b/programs/fuzz/fuzz_x509crl.c
index 00ad0bb454..d92cf5acd3 100644
--- a/programs/fuzz/fuzz_x509crl.c
+++ b/programs/fuzz/fuzz_x509crl.c
@@ -2,6 +2,16 @@
 #include "mbedtls/x509_crl.h"
 #include "fuzz_common.h"
 
+/* Initialise PSA once per process. Parsing does not draw random numbers, so the
+ * per-input psa_crypto_init() below is then a no-op and the state is not freed. */
+int LLVMFuzzerInitialize(int *argc, char ***argv)
+{
+    (void) argc;
+    (void) argv;
+    (void) psa_crypto_init();
+    return 0;
+}
+
 int LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput(const uint8_t *Data, size_t Size)
 {
 #ifdef MBEDTLS_X509_CRL_PARSE_C
@@ -25,7 +35,6 @@ int LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput(const uint8_t *Data, size_t Size)
 #endif /* !MBEDTLS_X509_REMOVE_INFO */
 
 exit:
-    mbedtls_psa_crypto_free();
     mbedtls_x509_crl_free(&crl);
 #else /* MBEDTLS_X509_CRL_PARSE_C */
     (void) Data;
